    },
    "body": "The fixed raw-text adapter now implements #1085's request, grammar, byte-span and typed-refusal contract while retaining the accepted reader/core, vocabulary, query and four-fact context. Independent curation and a reviewed comparison harness bind the source, inputs, artifacts, runtime, isolation and resource limits before withheld access.\n\nThe sole preparation returned **UNAVAILABLE_REFERENCE_REPLAY**. Authoring inputs were exact on 320/320 valid rows across all sixteen form/profile cells; all 16 refusal cases and two schema probes matched. The OS then denied `sandbox-exec` execution of the pinned Python interpreter before startup. There were zero model loads/forwards/optimizer updates. Withheld inputs remain sealed; worker readiness, effective isolation, full-output preservation and fresh-process replay are NOT_RUN. Supplied segmentation remains the qualified model entry.\n\nThis PR preserves exact preparation receipts, both independent input-authoring attempts, source/terminal reviews, and a bounded original-source audit of afflom's Prism, Atlas, LexLean, lean4-prod, GNAF and both matmul repositories. It updates current roadmap and claim pointers without revising #1079's weak-control result or #1082's descriptive limits. No dependency or accepted model source changed.\n\nValidation: static Python source parsing; independent verification of all 168 source-closure records and retained receipt identities; the declared authoring/readiness preparation; claim-wording and diff-integrity checks. Broad QA and model evaluations were not run. Required PR/queue checks are transport acknowledgements, not scientific verification.\n\nReferences #1094. Its model-comparison DoD remains incomplete, so it stays open and blocked by #1096, the separately scoped zero-forward runtime readiness repair. #973 remains open and #954 blocked. No automatic comparison retry or relaxed isolation policy is part of this delivery.\n",
